    "title": "Boston Celtics TV Schedule",
    "text": "See how to watch or stream Boston Celtics games throughout the 2025-26 NBA season with this TV schedule. (Full NBA schedule available here.) This site may earn commission on purchases made via this page. Friday, April 24 Time (UTC)Game / TV11:00 pmEastern Conference Quarterfinal2Boston Celtics vs 7Philadelphia 76ersGame 3Prime Video | TSN5Sunday, April 26 Time (UTC)Game / TV11:00 pmEastern Conference Quarterfinal2Boston Celtics vs 7Philadelphia 76ersGame 4NBC, PeacockTuesday, April 28 Time (UTC)Game / TV11:00 pmEastern Conference Quarterfinal7Philadelphia 76ers vs 2Boston CelticsGame 5ESPN, ESPN UnlimitedThursday, April 30 Time (UTC)Game / TVTBDEastern Conference Quarterfinal2Boston Celtics vs 7Philadelphia 76ersGame 6 - if necessaryTBDSaturday, May 2 Time (UTC)Game / TVTBDEastern Conference Quarterfinal7Philadelphia 76ers vs 2Boston CelticsGame 7 - if necessaryTBD No more upcoming games to show. How to Watch Boston Celtics Games With star Jayson Tatum expected to miss most or even all of the season due to injury, the Celtics are set for 29 national TV games during the 2025-26 season, including two on ABC, six on ESPN, ten on NBC Sports (including four exclusive to Peacock) and seven on Prime Video. Locally, the Celtics are set for 67 games on NBC Sports Boston. Viewing options presented below: UNCASVILLE, CT – OCTOBER 13: A close up view of a microphone with the NBC Sports Boston logo before the Naismith Basketball Hall of Fame exhibition college basketball game between the UConn Huskies and the Boston College Eagles on October 13, 2025, at Mohegan Sun Arena in Uncasville, CT. (Photo by Erica Denhoff/Icon Sportswire) Direct-to-Subscriber Platforms Local games (NBC Sports Boston): Peacock (in market only): NBC Sports Boston can be added to a Peacock subscription for $15/mo (on top of a base Peacock subscription of $8/mo). NBA League Pass (out-of-market only): All out-of-market locally televised games, plus NBA TV. Also available as a standalone purchase through Amazon Prime Video. National games (ESPN/ABC, NBC/Peacock and Prime Video): Peacock: All NBC Sports-produced games on the NBC broadcast network and Peacock. ESPN Unlimited: All ESPN-produced games on the ESPN cable networks and ABC. Disney+: Occasional simulcasts of ESPN-produced games. Amazon Prime Video: All Amazon-produced games on Prime Video, plus the ability to purchase NBA League Pass as an add-on. Cable and Streaming Bundles YouTube TV: All games on ESPN/ABC and the NBC broadcast network. Some Peacock-exclusive games will be available via NBCSN. (Peacock can also be purchased in full through YouTube Channels). Sponsored offer: Get $100 off YouTube TV ($20 off for 5 months) when you sign up today. New users only. Cancel anytime. Terms apply. Sling: All games on ESPN/ABC (ABC games will be on ESPN3); NBA League Pass available as an add-on. Fubo: All games on ESPN/ABC and the NBC broadcast network. DIRECTV (stream): All games on ESPN/ABC and the NBC broadcast network; NBA League Pass available as an add-on. Linear cable (ex. Dish Network, Xfinity, DIRECTV): All games on ESPN/ABC and the NBC broadcast network. Hulu + Live TV: All games on ESPN/ABC and the NBC broadcast network. In-Person See the Celtics in person at the TD Garden, or catch them on the road, by purchasing tickets from Vivid Seats, SeatGeek or Gametime.",
